(Title) Tj
T*
(Community-centered approach to reversing metabolic syndrome: 18-week results of an) Tj
T*
(integrated program combining exercise, education, and clinical support) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Community-based structured programs may effectively address metabolic syndrome, though) Tj
T*
(Latin American evidence remains limited. We evaluated an 18-week integrated program) Tj
T*
(combining three weekly supervised aerobic sessions, monthly health-education workshops,) Tj
T*
(and biweekly clinical monitoring in 80 adults with metabolic syndrome. Participants were) Tj
T*
(randomly assigned \(intervention n=33, control n=47\) and groups were balanced at baseline.) Tj
T*
(Intervention participants attended supervised sessions and educational activities) Tj
T*
(regularly; controls received customary care. Primary outcomes measured changes in fitness) Tj
T*
(capacity, body measurements, fasting glucose, lipid panel, and blood pressure. The) Tj
T*
(intervention group demonstrated greater gains in fitness capacity, reductions in waist) Tj
T*
(circumference and body weight, lower fasting glucose and triglycerides, improved blood) Tj
T*
(pressure, and favorable shifts in cholesterol fractions. Within the intervention group,) Tj
T*
(significant improvements in fitness, weight loss, fat mass reduction, and lean muscle gain) Tj
T*
(were evident. These results demonstrate that an integrated, accessible community program) Tj
T*
(can produce meaningful improvements across multiple cardiometabolic domains in adults with) Tj
T*
(metabolic syndrome.) Tj
